dm42 (ccplugins) — develop HP-42S-family RPN programs, the SwissMicros DM42n
first.

The plugin's own files are MIT-licensed (see LICENSE). It ships no third-party
code. When run, scripts/build.sh downloads and compiles on the local machine:

  • SwissMicros' fork of Free42 — GPL-2.0; Free42 is Copyright (C) 2004-2025
    Thomas Okken, the DM42 extensions are SwissMicros'. Fetched from
    github.com/swissmicros/free42 at commit
    a7c705e476cfd6d83d7d8b90042999f386367813 ("Version 3.3.10").

  • The Intel Decimal Floating-Point Math Library — BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c)
    2011 Intel Corp. — from the archive bundled with that fork, patched and
    built by the fork's own script.

The resulting dm42sim binary links this GPL-2.0 code and is therefore covered
by the GPL-2.0. It is built locally and is not distributed by this plugin.

scripts/sim/dm42sim.cc adapts behaviour of the DMCP front end in SwissMicros'
DM42PGM (github.com/swissmicros/DM42PGM at commit
3270592f2be6f6d0316e1a0f482a1faecc14aaa9, dm/dm42_fns.cc): the separate
hi-res graphics layer and when it is cleared, 2x2 drawing in the 200x120
mode, the saving and restoring of the core display around menus, the
treatment of menu labels, and the rule that keys 1-6 keep their functions
while F1-F6 act as the menu keys. It follows DM42PGM's names and logic for
these hooks. DM42PGM is distributed under this licence:

